Coyote vs. Acme is actually expanding for its second weekend, moving into 3,727 North American theaters compared with 3,575 during its opening weekend.

And considering what happened behind the scenes, that's pretty wild.

The movie opened at No. 2 domestically with $15.9 million, giving distributor Ketchup Entertainment its biggest opening ever.

Even crazier? This is the same movie Warner Bros. once planned to shelve completely.

Instead of disappearing into a vault, Coyote vs. Acme is now getting a real theatrical run - and audiences have the chance to decide what happens next.

So if you've been waiting years to see Wile E. Coyote finally get his moment on the big screen... this is your chance.</div></div>]]></description><guid>https://imgur.com/a/vNkyL8m</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[TheRainbowegoSweet007]]></dc:creator></item><item><title>Bless you DV fairies. I’m sure whoever pays your bills will one day tell you they’re proud of you. I mean it won’t be today, it won’t be tomorrow, or ever really… but I know that dream sustains you</title><link>https://imgur.com/gallery/QiQ7ikg</link><description><![CDATA[<div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/CCC15Vs.jpg" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div></div>]]></description><guid>https://imgur.com/a/QiQ7ikg</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[malbec]]></dc:creator></item><item><title>You wanna be a doctor in America? Pay $200K up front, train on 12-24hr shifts afterwards for pennies, then try to climb out of debt from middle of road clinic/hospital job.</title><link>https://imgur.com/gallery/80D1hNX</link><description><![CDATA[<div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/B9jAxhC.jpg" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div></div>]]></description><guid>https://imgur.com/a/80D1hNX</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[zoraniko]]></dc:creator></item><item><title>Gotta wonder who emboldened these assholes.</title><link>https://imgur.com/gallery/oY5ETkb</link><description><![CDATA[<div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/kE8Y0Mp.jpg" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div></div>]]></description><guid>https://imgur.com/a/oY5ETkb</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[sleeperkid]]></dc:creator></item><item><title>"Get off my plain!"</title><link>https://imgur.com/gallery/AAWFPGA</link><description><![CDATA[<div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/l3xMOPE.gif" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div><div>sassy mofo</div></div>]]></description><guid>https://imgur.com/a/AAWFPGA</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[SanchoLibre]]></dc:creator></item><item><title>This is the first time I've seen footage from this angle.</title><link>https://imgur.com/gallery/cpH7y4G</link><description><![CDATA[<div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/UbKvNts.gif" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div></div>]]></description><guid>https://imgur.com/a/cpH7y4G</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[CitizenK9]]></dc:creator></item><item><title>My Poor Kitty</title><link>https://imgur.com/gallery/vHJR6Q1</link><description><![CDATA[<div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/tJrcKkZ.png" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div><div>My 15 year old Tortoiseshell "Shelly" escaped from the house last Monday morning, and when we finally found her late in the evening she was not usher left hind leg. We rushed her to the emergency vet to get checked out and they found that her upper femur was shattered.</div><div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/rm38uVO.jpg" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div><div>She weirdly was not in much pain, she just wanted to eat and play like normal. But they zooted her up on the good drugs to be sure she was comfortable.</div><div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/oWVU02u.png" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div><div>Sadly, they said our only option was amputation. Shelly is over 15 years old, and we were so worried this would be too much for her to handle.</div><div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/nXju6jP.jpg" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div><div>All the vet staff were impressed with Shelly's great attitude, she loves everyone. The whole time she wanted cuddles and belly rubs. While getting assessed, they discovered she had a terrible UTI that showed no symptoms at all. It came up in her blood work and urinalysis. She was just days away from getting really sick. So we were able to start nipping that in the bud.</div><div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/JQXdIFO.png" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div><div>Nicole (nicnak044) Forbidden lottery numbers 4 5 4 6 2 5 3</div><div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/KYyNiX9.jpg" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div><div>Fresh out of surgery as a tripod. Her tail was wrapped to keep it clean. She's on strong pain killers and antibiotics for the next 10 days.</div><div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/10i6Y11.jpg" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div><div>I was so afraid the first few days as she would not eat or drink.</div><div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/jddEnEf.jpg" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div><div>But as of yesterday she is eating and drinking and going on short walks around the house with me! She's using the litter box and acting very normal! We have a cone for her but she has no interest in touching her stitches at all so far!</div><div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/6tJm4v8.jpg" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div><div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/x0CfGaV.png" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div><div>I have her in a crate to make sure she rests and the other cats don't bother her, so far they only want to comfort her. I set up a camera to keep an eye on here and make sure she is kept safe.

This entire ordeal cost us close to $7000, we don't have $7000... So times are going to be very tough for a while. (well, tougher, as it's already been pretty bad lately)</div></div>]]></description><guid>https://imgur.com/a/vHJR6Q1</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[QuanticChaos]]></dc:creator></item><item><title>Nature's Quality Control</title><link>https://imgur.com/gallery/iuARZNn</link><description><![CDATA[<div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/PsjgTuj.png" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div><div>Above Link https://vimeo.com/408820791</div></div>]]></description><guid>https://imgur.com/a/iuARZNn</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[McPuffinStuff]]></dc:creator></item><item><title>Meme Redistribution Center TM</title><link>https://imgur.com/gallery/sUAZwTW</link><description><![CDATA[<div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/MEkMyhj.jpg" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div><div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/HbLUkFB.jpg" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div><div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/wyWN2WH.png" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div><div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/1DQRMvl.jpg" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div><div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/q7BuKD2.jpg" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div><div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/r0hmRXJ.jpg" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div><div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/F3TYgtz.jpg" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div><div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/2QBVpF2.jpg" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div><div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/kNTBiw2.jpg" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div><div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/1hPThl6.jpg" style="max-width: 90