José Mejía Hernandez was walking to a bus stop one morning last month when two men in plain clothes got out of an unmarked car. He ran. He says he remembers a jolt from a stun gun and then waking up at George Washington University Hospital, where doctors found bleeding inside his skull. His lawyers gave police bystander video and statements from witnesses who saw an officer's vehicle hit him. ICE strapped an ankle monitor on him and let him go.

Homeland Security says a man whose only conviction is for public intoxication in 2020 went to the hospital "out of precaution." His lawyers released photos showing both eyes blackened and one side of his face scraped raw from cheekbone to lip. Virginia's attorney general said he would not look at the case without a police report. Nobody in government had filed one. 17 days after his arrest, Mejía Hernandez did.

